                <pb facs="0239" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg143"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>More railway destroyed. Protecting troops withdrawn. Chinese Government becoming
                    more helpless every day. Foreign troops will have to protect railways. Russian,
                    English, and Japanese are ready to do so. Twenty-four foreign war vessels are at
                    Taku. The United States has only one.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
